\title{SuSiEOut: fine-mapping when causal variants may be omitted}
\description{
SuSiEOut implements SuSiE-OUT, a summary-statistic fine-mapping model for
loci at which a causal variant may have been removed from the tested set,
for example by a minor allele frequency (MAF) threshold or a SNP-only
filter. Each sparse effect can be null, assigned to a tested variant, or
assigned to an omitted variant (an \emph{OUT state}). An omitted variant is
represented by its LD fingerprint: its correlations with the tested
variants, measured in a sequencing reference panel that contains it.
}
\section{Main functions}{

\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=susieout_fit]{susieout_fit()}} fits the model at one locus.
\item \code{\link[=susieout_fit_grid]{susieout_fit_grid()}} and \code{\link[=susieout_fit_nuisance_grid]{susieout_fit_nuisance_grid()}} average fits
over polygenic and LD-mismatch settings.
\item \code{\link[=susieout_candidate_support]{susieout_candidate_support()}} and \code{\link[=susieout_credible_sets]{susieout_credible_sets()}} summarize
a fit.
\item \code{\link[=susieout_simulate_locus]{susieout_simulate_locus()}} generates loci with known causal variants.
}
}

\section{Naming}{

Arguments and fields named \verb{examined_*} refer to tested variants;
\verb{excluded_*} and \verb{outside_*} refer to omitted variants.
}

\section{Acknowledgements}{

SuSiE-OUT builds directly on the Sum of Single Effects (SuSiE) model of
Wang, Sarkar, Carbonetto and Stephens (2020) and its summary-statistic
extension SuSiE-RSS (Zou, Carbonetto, Wang and Stephens, 2022), and
it reuses \code{susieR} as a reference implementation. We are grateful to the
SuSiE authors for making their methods and software openly available.
SuSiEOut is an independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed
by the SuSiE authors or the \code{susieR} maintainers.
}

